But I think the biggest and best payoffs come from trying to think about the problem from a higher level and adjust the problem space itself.
Converting next\_token to return only a symbol rather than a tuple cut our object allocations by more than half.
Questioning the code’s design itself is much harder, but I think reaps a greater benefit.],
  [Anyway, these are hacks I like to use!
If you want to play around with the lexer we’ve been building in this post, I’ve put the source code here .],
  [I hope you enjoyed this, and have a good day!],
